.nh
.TH "desync" "1" "Sep 2026" "desync" ""

.SH "نام (NAME)"
desync-completion-zsh \- Generate the autocompletion script for zsh


.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
\fBdesync completion zsh [flags]\fP


.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
Generate the autocompletion script for the zsh shell.

.PP
If shell completion is not already enabled in your environment you will need
to enable it.  You can execute the following once:

.EX
echo "autoload -U compinit; compinit" >> ~/.zshrc
.EE

.PP
To load completions in your current shell session:

.EX
source <(desync completion zsh)
.EE

.PP
To load completions for every new session, execute once:

.SS Linux:
.EX
desync completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_desync"
.EE

.SS macOS:
.EX
desync completion zsh > $(brew --prefix)/share/zsh/site-functions/_desync
.EE

.PP
You will need to start a new shell for this setup to take effect.


.SH "گزینه‌ها (OPTIONS)"
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for zsh

.PP
\fB--no-descriptions\fP[=false]
	disable completion descriptions


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	config file (default $HOME/.config/desync/config.json)

.PP
\fB--digest\fP="sha512-256"
	digest algorithm, sha512-256 or sha256

.PP
\fB--verbose\fP[=false]
	verbose mode


.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
\fBdesync-completion(1)\fP


.SH "تاریخچه (HISTORY)"
